--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BUG FOUND (live, 2026-08-19 04:37 UTC)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- sendEmailOtp passed NO emailRedirectTo -> supabase-js defaults the magic-link
  redirect to window.location.origin ALONE.
- On GitHub Pages the app lives at /resume-analyser/, so the link redirected to
  https://jeremygideonbareh.github.io/ (github.io ROOT) -> HTTP 404
  "Site not found · GitHub Pages" (confirmed live: page title + status 404,
  access_token stranded in the URL hash, app never loaded).
- F3 had passed on localhost:4173 only because origin+pathname happened to
  equal the app URL there; the deployed origin exposed the bug.

FIX (committed with this evidence):
- src/lib/auth-flow.ts: sendEmailOtp now passes
  options.emailRedirectTo = window.location.origin + window.location.pathname
  (guarded by typeof window !== 'undefined' for the node test env).
- src/lib/__tests__/auth-flow.test.ts: +1 regression test stubbing window as
  { origin: https://jeremygideonbareh.github.io, pathname: /resume-analyser/ }
  asserting emailRedirectTo = https://jeremygideonbareh.github.io/resume-analyser/
- Supabase uri_allow_list: added the trailing-slash variant
  https://jeremygideonbareh.github.io/resume-analyser/ alongside the existing
  no-slash entry (PATCH /v1/projects/mhkieytinkgouhvwrmbp/config/auth, HTTP 200,
  verified in GET response). NOTE: full-config PUT/PATCH is rejected (SMTP
  fields conflict with the built-in emailer) — send ONLY the field being changed.

